{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"208be44c0345c6bf","name":"card_unit_133rd_ironman","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_133rd_ironman","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"133rd IRONMAN","text":"Reveal: Deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ for each turn spent in the frontline.","flavorText":"The 133rd Infantry Regiment, nicknamed Ironman, is a unit of the 34th Infantry Division of the US Army. During WWII the division saw its first combat in French Algeria in 1942 as part of the Eastern Task Force. From there, they engaged in numerous battles in Tunisia, including the Battle of Hill 609. Due to heavy losses in North Africa the division skipped the invasion of Sicily, but it would instead later participate in the attack on the Italian mainland, landing at Salerno on September 9, 1943, as part of Operation Avalanche. The division's bravery and resilience were showcased in numerous engagements, including the battles along the Mignano Gap and the assault on Monte Cassino. Despite suffering heavy casualties, the division continued to push forward, ultimately playing a pivotal role in the liberation of Italy and the Allied victory in Europe.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_133rd_ironman","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_133rd_ironman_title","SourceString":"133rd IRONMAN","LocalizedString":"133rd IRONMAN"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_133rd_ironman_text","SourceString":"Reveal: Deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ for each turn spent in the frontline.","LocalizedString":"Reveal: Deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ for each turn spent in the frontline."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_133rd_ironman_history","SourceString":"The 133rd Infantry Regiment, nicknamed Ironman, is a unit of the 34th Infantry Division of the US Army. During WWII the division saw its first combat in French Algeria in 1942 as part of the Eastern Task Force. From there, they engaged in numerous battles in Tunisia, including the Battle of Hill 609. Due to heavy losses in North Africa the division skipped the invasion of Sicily, but it would instead later participate in the attack on the Italian mainland, landing at Salerno on September 9, 1943, as part of Operation Avalanche. The division's bravery and resilience were showcased in numerous engagements, including the battles along the Mignano Gap and the assault on Monte Cassino. Despite suffering heavy casualties, the division continued to push forward, ultimately playing a pivotal role in the liberation of Italy and the Allied victory in Europe.","LocalizedString":"The 133rd Infantry Regiment, nicknamed Ironman, is a unit of the 34th Infantry Division of the US Army. During WWII the division saw its first combat in French Algeria in 1942 as part of the Eastern Task Force. From there, they engaged in numerous battles in Tunisia, including the Battle of Hill 609. Due to heavy losses in North Africa the division skipped the invasion of Sicily, but it would instead later participate in the attack on the Italian mainland, landing at Salerno on September 9, 1943, as part of Operation Avalanche. The division's bravery and resilience were showcased in numerous engagements, including the battles along the Mignano Gap and the assault on Monte Cassino. Despite suffering heavy casualties, the division continued to push forward, ultimately playing a pivotal role in the liberation of Italy and the Allied victory in Europe."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn"],"hasCovert":true,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/CandidateArtwork/Summe